@startuml seq-18-audit-logs-query
title Audit Logs — Query with Pagination (Auditor Dashboard)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
autonumber

actor "Auditor\n(Angular)" as Auditor
participant "Gateway\n:9000" as GW
participant "Audit Service\n:9009" as AuditSvc
participant "AuditStore\n(ConcurrentLinked\nDeque)" as Store
participant "AuditStats\ncompute" as Stats

== Load stats (every 30s poll) ==

Auditor -> GW : GET /api/audit/stats\nBearer JWT (PERM_audit:read)
GW -> AuditSvc : lb://audit-service
AuditSvc -> Store : stats()\n7-day rolling window filter
Store -> Stats : compute:\n  total, writes, denied, active actors\n  perDay[7] (Mon…Sun counts)\n  outcome breakdown (allowed/denied/error)\n  top 6 actors by (reads + writes)
Stats --> AuditSvc : AuditStats record
AuditSvc --> Auditor : 200 { total, writeActions, deniedActions,\n  activeActors, perDay:[], dayLabels:[],\n  allowed, errored, topActors:[] }

== Query logs with search + outcome filter ==

Auditor -> GW : GET /api/audit/logs?q=detection-rules&outcome=Allowed&limit=200\nBearer JWT (PERM_audit:read)
GW -> AuditSvc : route
AuditSvc -> Store : query("detection-rules", "Allowed", "", 200)
Store -> Store : stream entries (newest first)\nfilter by outcome=="Allowed"\nfilter where actor|action|resource|details contains "detection-rules"\nlimit(200)
Store --> AuditSvc : List<AuditEntry> (max 200)
AuditSvc --> Auditor : 200 [ { id, timestamp, actor, role,\n  action, resource, outcome, ip, details } ]

note over Auditor : Angular audit-logs.ts:\n- client-side pagination (20 rows/page)\n- pagedLogs = computed slice\n- pageWindow computed with ellipsis\n- exportCsv() via URL.createObjectURL

== Paginate result (client-side) ==

Auditor -> Auditor : pageIndex = 0\ntotalPages = ceil(200 / 20) = 10\npagedLogs = logs.slice(0, 20)

Auditor -> Auditor : click Next →\npageIndex = 1\npagedLogs = logs.slice(20, 40)

== Export CSV ==

Auditor -> Auditor : exportCsv()\nbuild CSV string from all 200 entries\nnew Blob([csv], {type:"text/csv"})\nURL.createObjectURL → download\naudit-logs-2026-09-16.csv

@enduml
